and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lend a hand "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to help"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It feels great to lend a helping hand. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to do some volunteer work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "underprivileged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "lacking resources; poor"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've already spoken with a few of the underprivileged folks that we will be serving."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall on hard times"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lose money or to go through a difficult period"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For the most part they're wonderful people who have fallen on hard times. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "handbook"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small book that contains advice, information or rules"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should have read your volunteering handbook."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "leaflet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of paper that gives you information about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I got a few leaflets in the mail."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "junk mail "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "advertisements for products that are sent to people without being requested"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought it was junk mail, so I threw it out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "duty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " responsibility; task"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why don't you start with that while I get the team leader to make a list of duties for us?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le07ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Causative Verb: To Get"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The verb <span class=\"italic\">to get </span>has a couple of different meanings in English. It also has a causative meaning."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's review the uses of the verb<span class=\"italic\"> to get</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. To talk about things you receive or end up having or holding."}, {"type": "text", "content": "&nbsp; <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>the impression he wasn't happy. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. To talk about things you achieve or obtain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>a prize for having the best costume.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "3. To talk about a disease or ailment you contracted"}, {"type": "text", "content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>a cold after walking in the snow.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "4. To talk about entering or reaching a place."}, {"type": "text", "content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">got </span>to the station a half hour late.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use<span class=\"italic\"> get</span> as a causative verb as well. You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I'm so glad Candice <span class=\"strong\">got</span> you to do this with me!</span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Get + object + past participle (get something done)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got</span> my police check sent directly to them.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get </span>when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll get a senior volunteer to store my purse in one of the lockers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Why don't you start with that while I get the team leader to make a list of duties for us?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Necessity: Should/Ought to/Shall"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">shall</span> to talk about necessity in the present, past and future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should </span>and <span class=\"strong\">ought to + infinitive </span>express obligation and duty. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> should </span>when you offer a subjective opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I think you <span class=\"strong\">should leave</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I think you <span class=\"strong\">should leave</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">ought to </span>to refer to a more general and more objective opinion:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We <span class=\"strong\">ought to protect</span> endangered species."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to refer to past obligations and necessities, you add the modal <span class=\"italic\">have </span>to the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should have seen </span>a doctor.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">ought to have been </span>more careful.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">shall </span>to express formal rules and regulations or commands: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Visitors <span class=\"strong\">shall </span>be accompanied at all times by a security guard.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">shall </span>not kill.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "New volunteers shall be accompanied by a senior volunteer at all times."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I really should have read it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Absolutely, and we probably ought to scrub the countertops, right?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a place in your community where there is a need (i.e. homelessness, after-school education)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm ten ways in which you could help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Convert your notes into a one-paragraph proposal."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your proposal with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm volun